  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health vouchers at YRCS Hajjah facility/ GRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Strengthening Access to Essential Health Care Project in Hajjah, Yemen, led by the Yemen Red Crescent Society (YRCS) with support from the German Red Cross, is pilot initiative aimed at improving healthcare access for 355 vulnerable individuals including IDPs, host communities, and pregnant or lactating women through a combined health voucher and cash assistance approach.&#xa0;
The project links patients to the YRCS health facility in Hajjah which was previously supported by BRC and GRC. The project will provide support for maternal and surgical services using vouchers while covering transportation costs via cash transfers.&#xa0;
A service fee on selected procedures supports the facility&#x2019;s sustainability by contributing to operational costs. The initiative builds on CVA preparedness work supported by BRC and ICRC with an aim of also strengthening YRCS&#x2019;s capacity to independently manage cash and voucher assistance and use it for sectoral outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
